  "knowledgeArticles": [
    {
      "id": "kb-001",
      "title": "How to Connect to Corporate GlobalProtect / WireGuard VPN",
      "slug": "connect-to-corporate-vpn",
      "category": "Network & Connectivity",
      "tags": [
        "vpn",
        "remote-work",
        "wireguard",
        "globalprotect"
      ],
      "isPublic": true,
      "status": "published",
      "views": 482,
      "helpfulCount": 89,
      "notHelpfulCount": 3,
      "authorId": "usr-alex-tech",
      "authorName": "Alex Rivera",
      "createdAt": "2026-02-10T10:00:00Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-09-15T14:00:00Z",
      "content": "\n### Overview\nAll remote employees must connect via the corporate VPN gateway before accessing internal Git repositories, ERP databases, or staging clusters.\n\n### Step 1: Install the Client\n1. Visit `https://vpn.lakhanglobal.com` and sign in with your corporate SSO credentials.\n2. Download the client installer for Windows (MSI) or macOS (PKG).\n3. Follow the on-screen prompts. Note that macOS requires allowing system extension under **Settings > Privacy & Security**.\n\n### Step 2: Portal Address Configuration\n- **Primary Portal URL**: `vpn-us.lakhanglobal.com`\n- **EMEA Gateway**: `vpn-uk.lakhanglobal.com`\n- **Auth Method**: Corporate Okta Single Sign-On + Microsoft Authenticator Push notification.\n\n### Troubleshooting\n- If handshakes fail, verify you are not on hotel/airplane Wi-Fi blocking UDP port 443 / 500.\n- Switch to TCP Fallback mode in the app Preferences if strict firewalls drop UDP packets.\n    "
    },
    {
      "id": "kb-002",
      "title": "Self-Service Password Reset (SSPR) & Multi-Factor Auth Setup",
      "slug": "self-service-password-reset-mfa",
      "category": "Security & Access",
      "tags": [
        "password",
        "mfa",
        "security",
        "authenticator"
      ],
      "isPublic": true,
      "status": "published",
      "views": 890,
      "helpfulCount": 154,
      "notHelpfulCount": 5,
      "authorId": "usr-sarah-admin",
      "authorName": "Sarah Jenkins",
      "createdAt": "2026-01-20T08:00:00Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-01T11:30:00Z",
      "content": "\n### Resetting Your Account Password\nIf your corporate password has expired or is locked out:\n1. Navigate to `https://auth.lakhanglobal.com/reset`.\n2. Enter your primary email address.\n3. Authenticate using your Microsoft Authenticator biometric prompt or registered hardware FIDO2 key.\n4. Select a new password meeting policy: minimum 16 characters, uppercase, lowercase, numbers, and no previous 10 passwords reused.\n\n### Adding a Backup MFA Device\nAlways register a secondary phone number or security key to prevent lockouts during international travel.\n    "
    },
    {
      "id": "kb-003",
      "title": "Outlook 365 Indexing and Search Troubleshooting Guide",
      "slug": "outlook-search-indexing-fix",
      "category": "Software & Cloud Apps",
      "tags": [
        "outlook",
        "m365",
        "search",
        "email"
      ],
      "isPublic": true,
      "status": "published",
      "views": 312,
      "helpfulCount": 47,
      "notHelpfulCount": 2,
      "authorId": "usr-alex-tech",
      "authorName": "Alex Rivera",
      "createdAt": "2026-04-12T15:00:00Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-10-01T09:00:00Z",
      "content": "\n### Symptom\nSearch in Microsoft Outlook returns \"We are having trouble fetching results\" or CPU spikes to 100%.\n\n### Resolution Steps\n1. Open Windows **Control Panel > Indexing Options**.\n2. Click **Advanced**, then select **Rebuild Index**.\n3. In Outlook, navigate to **File > Account Settings > Data Files**, select your mailbox and click **Settings > Advanced**, ensuring \"Use Cached Exchange Mode\" is checked for 1 Year.\n4. Restart your workstation.\n    "
    },
    {
      "id": "kb-004",
      "title": "Connecting to Corporate High-Speed Wi-Fi (802.1X EAP-TLS)",
      "slug": "corporate-wifi-setup-8021x",
      "category": "Network & Connectivity",
      "tags": [
        "wifi",
        "network",
        "certificate",
        "802.1x"
      ],
      "isPublic": true,
      "status": "published",
      "views": 260,
      "helpfulCount": 39,
      "notHelpfulCount": 1,
      "authorId": "usr-elena-tech",
      "authorName": "Elena Rostova",
      "createdAt": "2026-03-05T12:00:00Z",
      "updatedAt": "2026-07-20T16:00:00Z",
      "content": "\n### SSID: `Lakhan-Corporate-Secure`\n- **Security Type**: WPA3-Enterprise (802.1X)\n- **EAP Method**: PEAP / MSCHAPv2 or EAP-TLS using your MDM machine certificate.\n- **Identity**: `username@lakhanglobal.com`\n- **Certificate Trust**: Verify root CA is `Lakhan Global Internal Root CA G3`.\n    "
    }
  ],
